/*
Problem: Sort Colors
Platform: LeetCode
Difficulty: Medium
Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/sort-colors/

Approach:
Use 3 pointers:
low = 0, mid = 0, high = n-1

0 → swap with low, low++, mid++
1 → mid++
2 → swap with high, high--

Important:
After swapping with high, DON'T increase mid.
The new value at mid still needs to be checked.

Mistake:
The tricky part is the 2 case.
After swap(nums[mid], nums[high]), only high--.
mid stays because the swapped element is not checked yet.

Pattern:
0, 1, 2 → Dutch National Flag

Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)
*/
